\section{Conclusion and future work}
As seen in the results of the experiments, either \textbf{Euclidean Distance} or \textbf{Mean Squared Error} cause almost the same behavior on a decentralized federated learning benchmark given the same parameters. The ability to regulate linearly how strict the coalition algorithm would be and the bonus of being implemented by default in most of the mathematical libraries, makes them seem as the most versatiles to use on this type of work.

There are other similarity measures with different properties, and other types to apply them to the weights, in a way to attempt to take in consideration the topology of the neural network during the calculations of similarity. We leave these questions on future work.

